"""Generate concise documentation and claim/provenance records from shipped registries."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
locations=json.loads((ROOT/'data/locations.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
terrain=json.loads((ROOT/'public/processed/jezero.json').read_text())
audit=json.loads((ROOT/'data/audit.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
validation=json.loads((ROOT/'data/validation/independent.json').read_text())
claims=[{'id':l['id']+'-summary','claim':l['summary'],'sourceIds':[l['id']],'sourceUrls':[l['sourceUrl']],'locationId':l['id'],'status':'source-linked; automated retrieval completed' if l['sourceStatus'].startswith('retrieved') else 'source-linked; automated access incomplete','evidenceSection':'Original source description / caption','uncertainty':l['coordinateNote']} for l in locations]
(ROOT/'data/claims.json').write_text(json.dumps(claims,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False),encoding='utf-8')
provenance={'dataset':terrain,'originalLocalAudit':next(r for r in audit if r['format']=='.tif'),'script':'scripts/gis/process_terrain.py','resampling':'None for regional elevations; average for global 720×360 MOLA overview','transformations':'Mars equirectangular projected metres ↔ planetocentric latitude/east longitude. Original rasters preserved.','outputs':[{'file':p.name,'bytes':p.stat().st_size} for p in (ROOT/'public/processed').iterdir() if p.is_file()]}
(ROOT/'data/provenance.json').write_text(json.dumps(provenance,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False),encoding='utf-8')
sources='# Scientific data sources\n\nCore products: [NASA Mars Trek WMTS](https://trek.nasa.gov/tiles/apidoc/trekAPI.html?body=mars), [MOLA DEM](https://astrogeology.usgs.gov/search/map/mars_mgs_mola_dem_463m), [CTX DTM]('+terrain['sourcePage']+'), [IAU/USGS coordinates](https://planetarynames.wr.usgs.gov/SearchResults?Target=20_Mars), [MCD context](https://www-mars.lmd.jussieu.fr/mars/access).\n\n'
sources+='\n'.join(f"- **{l['id']} / {l['name']}**: [{l['mission']}]({l['sourceUrl']}); [coordinate evidence]({l['coordinateSource']}). Accessed {l['accessed']}. Status: {l['sourceStatus']}." for l in locations)
sources+='\n\nSoftware documentation is distinct from scientific evidence: [Next.js static exports](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/guides/static-exports), [OpenLayers](https://openlayers.org/en/latest/apidoc/), [Rasterio](https://rasterio.readthedocs.io/).\n'
(ROOT/'docs/DATA_SOURCES.md').write_text(sources,encoding='utf-8')
(ROOT/'docs/SCIENTIFIC_CLAIMS.md').write_text('# Scientific claims register\n\nThe machine-readable register is `data/claims.json`. It includes claim text, source IDs and URLs, evidence section, location, verification/access status and uncertainty. Source-linked is not a claim of peer review or verification of every sentence in the original supplied research.\n\n'+'\n'.join(f"- **{c['id']}**: {c['claim']} [Evidence]({c['sourceUrls'][0]}). {c['status']}." for c in claims)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
(ROOT/'docs/DATA_PROVENANCE.md').write_text('# Dataset provenance\n\nFull machine-readable records: `data/provenance.json`, `data/audit.json`, `public/processed/jezero.json`.\n\n## Regional CTX terrain\n\n- Original URL: '+terrain['sourceUrl']+'\n- Acquired: '+terrain['acquired']+'\n- SHA-256: `'+terrain['sha256']+'`\n- Preserved source: ignored `data/raw/jezero-ctx-20m.tif`\n- Processing: `scripts/gis/process_terrain.py`\n- Grid: 1596 × 1512, 20 m projected pixel spacing; R=3396190 m, native equirectangular transform.\n- Nodata: extreme negative float32 sentinel and nonfinite values excluded before arithmetic.\n- Elevation resampling: none.\n- Outputs: little-endian float32 elevations/slopes, uint8 valid mask, metadata JSON, labelled derivative elevation image.\n- Units: metres elevation / degrees slope.\n- Details and limitations: '+terrain['processing']+'\n\n## Global MOLA\n\nThe supplied original is preserved and checksummed in `data/audit.json`. Rasterio creates a 720×360 average numerical overview (0.5° cells), preserving nodata. The original is never bundled. Global relief imagery comes from NASA Trek, a distinct visualization source.\n\n## Images\n\nOriginal source-page image URLs and access dates are stored in `data/locations.json`. Derivatives preserve content, reduce maximum dimensions to 1100×700, and encode JPEG quality 88. No geographic details are generated. Source screenshots remain untouched and excluded from quantitative use.\n',encoding='utf-8')
(ROOT/'docs/IMAGE_CREDITS.md').write_text('# Image credits\n\nIllustrations are source-page derivatives, not necessarily natural-colour photographs or whole-region views. Follow each original caption for location/coverage, observation date, processing, exact institutional credit and usage terms. No blanket relicensing is asserted.\n\n'+'\n'.join(f"- **{l['name']}**: derivative `{l['image']}`; [original image]({l['imageSource']}); [caption, credits and usage]({l['sourceUrl']}); accessed {l['accessed']}." for l in locations if l['image'])+'\n\nNo image is shown for a location whose source-page image was not retrieved. This avoids misidentifying a supplied, unverified file as an authenticated site photograph. All supplied images remain recorded in the audit.\n',encoding='utf-8')
rows='\n'.join(f"| {r['case']} | {r['route']} | {r['distanceM']:.2f} | {r['maxSlopeDegrees']:.2f} | {r['absoluteCostDifference']:.2g} |" for r in validation['results'])
(ROOT/'docs/VALIDATION.md').write_text('# Validation record\n\n## Checks actually run\n\n- TypeScript check: passed.\n- ESLint: passed without warnings after image/config fixes.\n- Vitest: 8 tests passed (controlled coordinates/terrain plus one test covering three real-terrain endpoint pairs and six routes).\n- Independent Python Dijkstra: all six route costs agree within 0.0001 model-cost metres; distances independently agree within 0.0001 m. Original GeoTIFF spot samples match exported elevation cells.\n- Production static build: passed locally and on Vercel.\n- Early deployed atlas: 2 Playwright tests passed against production; NASA tile responses, all 13 destinations, search, source filtering, coordinates, layer controls and mobile selection.\n- Updated local static export: 4 Playwright tests passed, including desktop/mobile endpoint dragging, worker recalculation, comparisons, explanation/export and stale-metric clearing.\n- Final production suite: pending the final release deployment; record the actual result below when run.\n\n## Independent real-terrain results\n\n| Case | Mode | Distance (m) | Maximum modelled slope (°) | Absolute independent cost difference |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n'+rows+'\n\nInputs and complete paths are recorded in `data/validation/routes.json`; independent results are in `data/validation/independent.json`. Source checksum: `'+terrain['sha256']+'`. Reproduce with `npm test`, then `scripts/validation/verify_routes.py` after source acquisition.\n\n## What these checks establish\n\nThe two implementations agree on numerical terrain costs and distance. These are not comparisons with recorded astronaut traverses or field-certified safe routes. High-resolution imagery/elevation registration is based on published co-registered product extents and compatible CRS, not a new independent control-network accuracy assessment. Browser tests are Chromium automation; other browser engines and long-term NASA service availability are not validated.\n',encoding='utf-8')
